# CODEOWNERS — path ownership map for overboard-web
#
# Ported from the sibling `overboard` repo on 2026-07-31, under the countersign
# agreed 2026-07-28: the COO authors this file, the CMO proposes the path→role
# assignments inside it. Every assignment below is the CMO's, from overboard#118
# and the countersign row — not the COO's invention. Where nothing was proposed,
# nothing has been assigned; see "Deliberately unassigned" at the bottom.
#
# Roles are defined in `overboard/docs/decisions/ROLES.md`, which is the single
# home for the role list. The `# role:` tag above each rule is the authoritative
# assignment.
#
# ⚠️ THE TAGS ARE NOT YET MACHINE-CHECKED IN THIS REPO. In `overboard`,
# `policy_check.py` validates every tag against the registry and fails the build
# on a trespass — that gate has not been ported here yet, so today this file is
# a documented map rather than an enforced one. Porting the gate is the other
# half of the countersign and is tracked separately. Do not read a green build
# here as "no trespass"; nothing is checking.
#
# GitHub CODEOWNERS can only name real accounts and this org has one human, so
# @MikePaNtZ is the reviewer on every rule. CODEOWNERS provides no review
# routing here — the tags are what carry meaning. Do not remove them.
#
# OWNERSHIP GOVERNS WRITE, NOT READ. Reading or linking to another role's file
# needs no permission and no row. Only editing does.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so specific rules go BELOW general ones.
# See overboard/docs/decisions/ADR-0002-path-ownership-map.md.

